6. No advice, no warranty
19 Degrees is an independent educational and research project. Its text, charts, data and code summarise public data and published research. They may contain errors or be out of date and are provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. They are not safety, medical, legal or professional advice. Don't rely on them to decide whether or where to swim, surf or dive: follow lifesavers, beach signs and local authorities. Product information summarises published independent tests, which are linked; it is not the author's own testing and is not an endorsement or a criticism of any maker. To the fullest extent the law allows, the author is not liable for any loss, injury or damage arising from use of, or reliance on, this project or anything built with it. Anyone who reuses the code, data or content (for example in an app, alert or warning service) is responsible for how they use it.

